One prominent AI company is **DeepMind**, a British artificial intelligence subsidiary of Alphabet Inc. (Google's parent company). Founded in 2010 and acquired by Google in 2014, DeepMind is renowned for developing groundbreaking AI systems such as:  
- **AlphaGo**, which defeated world champion Go players;    
- **AlphaFold**, which revolutionized protein structure prediction for biological research;  
- **Gemini**, a multimodal large language model (LLM) family.    

DeepMind focuses on advancing general artificial intelligence (AGI) while emphasizing safety and ethical AI development.  

Other notable AI companies include **OpenAI** (known for GPT models and ChatGPT), **Anthropic** (Claude LLM), **Meta AI** (Llama models), and **NVIDIA** (AI hardware and software infrastructure).

The PlayStation 5 (PS5), developed by Sony Interactive Entertainment, is a leading example. Launched in November 2020, it represents the ninth generation of home video game consoles. Key features include:

- **Custom hardware** with an AMD Zen 2 CPU and RDNA 2 GPU delivering 10.3 teraflops of power;
- **Ultra-high-speed SSD** drastically reducing load times (up to 5.5GB/s raw throughput);
- **DualSense controller** with haptic feedback and adaptive triggers for immersive tactile responses;
- **Tempest 3D AudioTech** for spatial sound.

Unlike its predecessors, the PS5 emphasizes near-instant game loading and ray-tracing support for lifelike lighting. (Note: While alternatives like the Xbox Series X or Nintendo Switch exist, the PS5 is highlighted here as a representative choice.)
